Synthesize ALL skill/tool creation results into a comprehensive **Role Setup Report** in Markdown. This report documents the complete setup of an AI employee role — what was associated, what was created, and how everything connects.

### Required Sections

## 1. Role Summary
Brief overview of the role being set up: name, purpose, primary responsibilities, and organizational fit. Reference the original role document.

## 2. Existing Tools Associated
For each tool already in the system that maps to a role need:
- Tool name and current description
- Which role responsibility/SOP it supports
- Any configuration or customization needed for this role
- Present as a table: | Tool | Role Need | Configuration |

## 3. New Tools/Skills Created
For each newly created tool/skill, summarize:
- **Name** and **description**
- **Parameters** (key inputs)
- **What it does** (in 2-3 sentences)
- **Which role responsibility/SOP** it supports
- **Implementation approach** (API calls, integrations, etc.)
- **Key design decisions** from the research

## 4. SOPs & Workflow Wiring
For each SOP in the role document, map which tools (existing + new) support each step:
- Present as a table: | SOP Step | Tool(s) | How Used |
- Identify any SOP steps that remain manual (no tool support)
- Note workflow sequences where tools should be chained

## 5. Gaps & Future Work
- Capabilities from the role document that are NOT fully addressed by any tool
- Tools that were created but may need further refinement
- Integration points that need engineering work beyond the tool specification
- Prioritized list of follow-up items

## 6. Verification Plan
- For each new tool: example invocation and expected output
- End-to-end test scenarios: "Given [role task], the role should be able to [use tool X to achieve Y]"
- Metrics: how to measure whether the role setup is effective

### Quality Requirements
- **Traceability**: Every tool association/creation should trace back to a specific role document section
- **Completeness**: The report should account for ALL tools, skills, and capabilities referenced anywhere in the role document — including those mentioned in responsibilities, SOPs, and collaboration patterns
- **Actionability**: The report should be usable by an engineer to implement the remaining wiring
- **No duplication**: If the same tool serves multiple role needs, list it once and cross-reference
